  "theorem_name": "WeightedPrimePowerEnvelopeAndFactorTwoBudgetReduction",
  "declared_proposition": "Let W_pp(X)=sum_{p^k<=X,k>=2} log p. The proper-prime-power part E_pp(N) of the binary von Mangoldt correlation satisfies E_pp(N)<=2 log(N) W_pp(N). If A(N) counts proper prime powers, then W_pp(N)<=A(N)log(N)/2 and hence E_pp(N)<=A(N)(log N)^2, halving the corresponding count-based factor in the TICKET-191 sufficient budget.",
  "mathematical_argument": "Charge each contaminated ordered pair to a proper prime power in its left or right coordinate. The other von Mangoldt factor is at most log N, giving the first union bound. For q=p^k with k>=2 and q<=N, log p=log q/k<=log N/2. Summing over the A(N) proper powers gives the second bound. Strict total correlation above this envelope leaves positive prime-prime mass.",
